    <keyword>SET INDEX command<keyword>FoxPro</keyword></keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET INDEX Command &#160;(FoxPro)</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Opens one or more index files for the current table and optionally selects the controlling order. This is the FoxPro version of the <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_INDEX">SET INDEX</link> command.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET INDEX TO [&lt;IndexFile1&gt; [, &lt;IndexFile2&gt; ...]]<br/> &#160; [ORDER [TAG &lt;OrderName&gt; [OF &lt;IndexFile&gt;]]] [ASCENDING | DESCENDING] [ADDITIVE]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">&lt;IndexFile1&gt;, ...<tab />The index files to open. If the list is omitted (SET INDEX TO without arguments), all open index files for the current table are closed.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ORDER [TAG] &lt;OrderName&gt; [OF &lt;IndexFile&gt;]<tab />Selects the controlling order after the index files have been opened.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ASCENDING | DESCENDING<tab />Changes the direction of the controlling order.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ADDITIVE<tab />Keeps the index files that are already open open. Without this clause, the other index files are closed before the new files are opened.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Examples</para>
    <para styleclass="Code Example">USE Customers<br/>
SET INDEX TO Customers.cdx ORDER TAG LastName DESCENDING<br/>
SET INDEX TO Extra.cdx ADDITIVE</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibRT" inline="false"/></para>
